  "summary": "The fifth proposal's fix — making all push paths consistently use unfiltered FeatureFile.list_all() — correctly identifies the oscillation mechanism but introduces a worse problem: it means the server always holds a cross-board superset for every client, so the /api/board endpoint (api.go:411-417) will return duplicate features when multiple TUI clients on the same board are connected, since it naively concatenates all clients' feature lists with no deduplication. The real issue is that hub.go:354 does a flat unconditional replace with no concept of board identity, while the /api/board aggregation at api.go:411-417 assumes each client's feature list is a non-overlapping partition. Making all pushes unfiltered guarantees overlap and duplication in the webui. The correct minimal fix is two-fold: (1) make ALL client-side push paths use the same board-filtered call (_load_features(self.active_board)) at lines 2093, 2137, and 2636 so every push is consistently scoped — this eliminates the oscillation between full and filtered snapshots that causes the flickering — and (2) the comment at line 2634 ('push ALL features for aggregate view') reflects a misunderstanding of the server architecture, since /api/board already aggregates across clients, so each client only needs to contribute its own board's features for the aggregate to work correctly. The fifth proposal's concern that filtered pushes would break the aggregate view is wrong: if client A pushes board-X features and client B pushes board-Y features, /api/board returns both boards' features via client aggregation — that's the designed aggregation path, not intra-client cross-board pushes."
